{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/crossvalidationfolds"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Evaluate model stability and generalization performance across dataset splits using ","type":"text"},{"code":"KFold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"StratifiedKFold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeSeriesSplit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/HyperparameterTuning","doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/ParallelModelSelection"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftOptimize"}],"title":"Cross-Validation Strategies","roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/CrossValidationFolds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-validation is essential for estimating the out-of-sample prediction error and hyperparameter tuning without data leakage. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftOptimize"},{"type":"text","text":" generates zero-allocation index pairs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(trainIndices, validationIndices)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of duplicating dataset matrices in memory."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Index-Based Split Architecture","level":3,"anchor":"Index-Based-Split-Architecture","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each split strategy implements deterministic or seeded index generation:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["Dataset (N samples)","┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐","│ Fold 1: [ Val (20%) ] [                Train (80%)        ] │","│ Fold 2: [ Train (20%) ] [ Val (20%) ] [ Train (60%)       ] │","│ Fold 3: [ Train (40%) ] [ Val (20%) ] [ Train (40%)       ] │","│ Fold 4: [ Train (60%) ] [ Val (20%) ] [ Train (20%)       ] │","│ Fold 5: [                Train (80%)        ] [ Val (20%) ] │","└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"1. Standard K-Fold Cross-Validation","level":2,"anchor":"1-Standard-K-Fold-Cross-Validation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KFold"},{"type":"text","text":" splits continuous regression data or balanced observations into $K$ contiguous or randomized partitions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftDataFrame","import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Prepare synthetic features and targets","let sampleCount = 100","let featureCount = 4","let X = (0..<sampleCount).map { row in","    (0..<featureCount).map { col in Double(row * featureCount + col) * 0.05 }","}","let y = X.map { row in row.reduce(0.0, +) * 1.5 + 2.0 }","","\/\/ 2. Configure 5-fold cross-validation with a fixed random seed","let kfold = KFold(nSplits: 5, shuffle: true, randomSeed: 42)","let splits = kfold.split(X: X)","","print(\"Generated \\(splits.count) validation folds.\")","","\/\/ 3. Train and evaluate linear regressors across folds","var mseScores: [Double] = []","","for (foldIndex, (trainIndices, valIndices)) in splits.enumerated() {","    let trainX = trainIndices.map { X[$0] }","    let trainY = trainIndices.map { y[$0] }","    let valX = valIndices.map { X[$0] }","    let valY = valIndices.map { y[$0] }","    ","    let model = LinearRegression(learningRate: 0.01, epochs: 200)","    try await model.fit(features: trainX, targets: trainY)","    ","    let predictions = try await model.predict(features: valX)","    let mse = try RegressionMetrics.meanSquaredError(yTrue: valY, yPred: predictions)","    mseScores.append(mse)","    ","    print(\"Fold \\(foldIndex + 1): MSE = \\(String(format: \"%.4f\", mse))\")","}","","let meanMSE = mseScores.reduce(0.0, +) \/ Double(mseScores.count)","print(\"Average Cross-Validation MSE: \\(String(format: \"%.4f\", meanMSE))\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"2. Stratified K-Fold for Classification","level":2,"anchor":"2-Stratified-K-Fold-for-Classification","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StratifiedKFold"},{"type":"text","text":" ensures that every validation fold preserves the exact class label distribution proportions of the entire dataset. This is critical for imbalanced target classes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Dataset with imbalanced binary classes (80% Class 0, 20% Class 1)","let features = (0..<100).map { i in [Double(i), Double(i * 2)] }","let labels = (0..<100).map { $0 < 80 ? 0 : 1 }","","\/\/ 2. Initialize Stratified K-Fold","let stratifiedKF = StratifiedKFold(nSplits: 5, shuffle: true, randomSeed: 123)","let folds = stratifiedKF.split(X: features, y: labels)","","for (idx, (trainIdx, valIdx)) in folds.enumerated() {","    let valLabels = valIdx.map { labels[$0] }","    let class1Count = valLabels.filter { $0 == 1 }.count","    let class0Count = valLabels.filter { $0 == 0 }.count","    ","    print(\"Fold \\(idx + 1): Class 0 = \\(class0Count), Class 1 = \\(class1Count) (Ratio: \\(Double(class1Count)\/Double(valLabels.count)))\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"3. Expanding-Window TimeSeriesSplit","level":2,"anchor":"3-Expanding-Window-TimeSeriesSplit","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For temporal and sequential datasets, standard random cross-validation introduces data leakage (evaluating on historical data after training on future observations). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeSeriesSplit"},{"type":"text","text":" creates expanding historical training windows with forward-looking validation sets."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftForecast","","let timeSeriesData = (0..<120).map { i in Double(i) * 1.2 + sin(Double(i) * 0.2) }","","let tsSplit = TimeSeriesSplit(nSplits: 4, maxTrainSize: nil)","let temporalFolds = tsSplit.split(dataCount: timeSeriesData.count)","","for (foldIndex, (trainIdx, valIdx)) in temporalFolds.enumerated() {","    print(\"Fold \\(foldIndex + 1): Train [\\(trainIdx.first!)...\\(trainIdx.last!)] (\\(trainIdx.count) pts) -> Val [\\(valIdx.first!)...\\(valIdx.last!)] (\\(valIdx.count) pts)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Performance Tip:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Always access data via index arrays ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trainIndices.map { X[$0] }"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than cloning full matrices up front. This keeps memory footprints proportional to the active batch size."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftOptimize/documentation/SwiftOptimize/HyperparameterTuning":{"role":"article","title":"Hyperparameter Tuning & AutoML Engine","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Automate model exploration and parameter optimization with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridSearchCV"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RandomizedSearchCV"},{"type":"text","text":", and the intelligent "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoML"},{"type":"text","text":" model selector."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/hyperparametertuning","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/HyperparameterTuning","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftOptimize/documentation/SwiftOptimize/ParallelModelSelection":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/ParallelModelSelection","type":"topic","title":"Concurrent Model Selection & Cross-Validation","url":"\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/parallelmodelselection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Harness all available Apple Silicon CPU and GPU cores using structured Swift Concurrency "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" primitives."}]},"doc://SwiftOptimize/documentation/SwiftOptimize":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize","url":"\/documentation\/swiftoptimize","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"SwiftOptimize","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"AutoML, Cross-Validation Folds & Hyperparameter Tuning."}],"type":"topic"}}}